<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernkastel-Kues</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bernkastel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernkastel-Kues is a wine town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, formed in 1905 from Bernkastel and Kues on opposite banks. Above it stands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> castle, built by the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>, and Kues was the birthplace of the philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-of-cusa">Nicholas of Cusa</a>. Its Doctor vineyard is among the most famous on the Moselle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernkastel-kues.jpg" alt="Bernkastel-Kues" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_image_of_the_Moselle_in_Bernkastel-Kues_(view_from_the_southeast).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
